    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\ncopilot-language-server prefetches the suggestion that follows the one on screen, but only once the client reports it as shown with `textDocument/didShowCompletion`. Core rightly doesn't send that, since it isn't in the spec, but there's also no public way to know when `vim.lsp.inline_completion` shows an item, so sending it means wrapping the private `Completor:select`. Without it, the suggestion after an accept is a fresh round trip, 222-286 ms here against 3-5 ms from the prefetch (copilot-language-server 1.554.0).\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nA public hook when an item is shown, like `get()`'s `on_accept`, either a callback or an autocmd, so a config or plugin can send the server's notification itself.\n",
